the knowledge base implies_example includes:

the text of the source program is at "sources/implies-example.l4".

implies version for a boolean with a second boolean if
    it is not the case that true is equal to the boolean
    or true is equal to the second boolean.

else version for a value with a second value if
    it is not the case that
        true is equal to the value
        or true is equal to the second value.

badge rule if
    it is not the case that is employee
    or has badge.

consent rule if
    it is not the case that
        the person age is a number N
        and N < 18
    or has parental consent.

chained impl for a boolean with a second boolean with a third boolean if
    it is not the case that true is equal to the boolean
    or true is equal to the third boolean
        or it is not the case that true is equal to the second boolean.

conjunction implies for a boolean with a second boolean with a third boolean if
    it is not the case that
        true is equal to the boolean
        and true is equal to the second boolean
    or true is equal to the third boolean.

implies disjunction for a value with a second value with a third value if
    it is not the case that true is equal to the value
    or true is equal to the second value
        or true is equal to the third value.

